    "result": "I implemented `encode` and `decode` in `solution.py`, keeping the stub's signatures, and made no other changes. `encode` scans maximal runs: runs of four or more become `~<n>~<c>`, and shorter runs are written character by character, with `~` escaped as `~~`. `decode` reads left to right: `~~` yields one `~`, a `~` followed by digits becomes a run, and every malformed case raises `ValueError` as the spec lists (dangling `~`, invalid character after `~`, leading zero, count below 4, missing `~` after the count, missing run character). Digits are matched against an explicit `0`–`9` set rather than `str.isdigit()`, so non-ASCII digits are rejected. As instructed, I did not run or test the code.",
